    nested_use_in_it_block_cannot_resolve_transitive_enums_2026-09-05, 1, "revalidated 2026-11-02 (close-invalid lane): action=fixed_pending_verification NOT confirmed - no merged fix commit or passing regression cited in the bug doc or git history; keep open"
    nested_use_in_it_block_cannot_resolve_transitive_enums_2026-09-05, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: claim released back to open - defect is in the Rust seed module loader, outside this lane's constraints. Evidence: synthetic 3-module transitive chains (enum+fn, glob/selective/private, with/without overlap) all PASS through nested use - shallow transitivity works; the real repro (plan-acceptance spec with uses moved back into its blocks) fails 3/5 with function vhdl_kernel_accepts not found. SIMPLE_LOADER_TRACE=1 (17953 events) shows vhdl_kernel_entity.spl is never resolved/loaded on the nested path; vhdl_kernel_accepts is a private fn reachable only via the compiler/backend/vhdl facade re-exports which go circular-partial in this closure; the nested lane's unprovided/private-use check fails soft (warn-once-and-continue, module_loader.rs:1183-1194) so names are silently never bound; miss surfaces via simple_interp_call E3008. File-scope works because the whole closure registers with whole-surface+private baselining (module_loader.rs:1148-1153). Pure-Simple cannot touch this path (marker prints in spec.spl to_equal and module_resolver/resolution.spl produced zero output during nested resolution; every diagnostic traces to compiler_rust). Ready-made acceptance spec kept at build/p3cache/nesteduse/renested_plan_spec.spl. Seed-lane fix direction: bind private-baselined names from resolved modules on the nested path (or propagate the unprovided error), resolve facade re-export targets past circular-partial."

